<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Progress Billing & Valuations</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Accelerate cash flow with structured valuation processes that ensure billing accurately reflects work 
            completed on site and "materials on site".
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Digital Monthly Valuations</h2>
        <p>
            The billing module streamlines the monthly valuation process through a structured interface for 
            measuring progress against technical specifications and the BOQ. Quantify physical work-in-progress, 
            percentage completions, and "materials on site" according to specific contract terms. By 
            linking claims directly to site diary entries and inspection photos, the system provides 
            the "evidence of work" needed to minimize client queries and accelerate certification.
        </p>
        <p>
            Standardized valuation templates ensure consistency across the project portfolio, allowing 
            quantity surveyors and project managers to review and authorize claims within an 
            audit-compliant workflow before they are submitted to the client.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Interim Payment Certificates (IPC)</h2>
        <p>
            Automate the generation of formal Interim Payment Certificates (IPC) and applications for payment 
            (AFP) directly from validated site data. The system automatically calculates retention 
            deductions, advances, and previously certified amounts, eliminating the arithmetic errors 
            that lead to commercial friction and payment delays.
        </p>
        <p>
            Track the status of every application through the entire lifecycle—from submission to 
            certification and final cash receipt. Integrated aging reports for certified IPCs allow 
            the finance team to focus collection efforts on accounts approaching contractual 
            payment deadlines, ensuring project liquidity is maintained.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Retention and Financial Release</h2>
        <p>
            Manage the complexities of project retentions with automated registers that track cumulative 
            held amounts for both the main contract and all subcontracts. Detailed retention schedules 
            provide visibility into upcoming milestones for partial (practical completion) and 
            final (defects liability) releases.
        </p>
        <p>
            Integrated cash flow forecasting combines these retention release dates with project 
            billing cycles and operational costs, providing a multi-month view of net project 
            cash flow. This intelligence allows the organization to optimize its working 
            capital and plan for the financial requirements of future project phases.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

